From: SM-X910 postmarketOS port <gts9uwifi@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: don't defer external DP for unresolved USB-C bridge

The SM-X910 routes DisplayPort through a QMP combo PHY and PS5169 Type-C
retimer to a usb-c-connector node.  The connector is not a DRM bridge, so the
transparent bridge chain ends in -EPROBE_DEFER.  Deferring the DP component
also prevents the shared MSM DRM component master and the unrelated internal
DSI panel from binding.

External DP already has complete detect, HPD, EDID and mode operations in the
MSM DP bridge.  Treat an unresolved optional downstream bridge like no
downstream bridge for external DP.  Keep eDP strict because its panel bridge
is mandatory.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1016,7 +1016,8 @@ static int msm_dp_display_probe_tail(struct device *dev)
 	if (IS_ERR(dp->next_bridge)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(dp->next_bridge);
 		dp->next_bridge = NULL;
-		if (dp->is_edp || ret != -ENODEV)
+		if (dp->is_edp ||
+		    (ret != -ENODEV && ret != -EPROBE_DEFER))
 			return ret;
 	}
 
